{"imf":{"id":"34656ba8-47d9-433e-80c8-d2bb0f75741f","word":"IMF","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"International Monetary Fund","tags":["masculine"],"word":"FMI"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Now I tried to make amends, small talk, but he was busy with a huge sheaf of papers, on which I spotted graphs I couldn’t follow, sets of statistics from the IMF.","ref":"2016, Zadie Smith, Swing Time, New York, N.Y.: Penguin Press, →ISBN, pages 194–195:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[158,161]],"id":"99fbd917-721d-4503-8cac-d69bc4b27785"},{"text":"The prospects for the global economy as outlined by the IMF are the third weakest since 2001, behind only the 2008 financial crisis and the worst phase of the coronavirus pandemic. Global growth has fallen below 2% just five times since 1970.","ref":"2022 October 11, Julia Horowitz, “‘The worst is yet to come’: IMF issues stark recession warning”, in CNN Business, archived from the original on 05 Aug 2025:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[56,59]],"id":"3a08db75-59b2-4ae6-a629-6e936e6bc5ba"},{"text":"The OECD expects inflation to remain above 9% this year among advanced economies. It’s then forecast to fall back to 6.6% in 2023, slightly above levels forecast by the IMF.","ref":"2022 November 22, Hanna Ziady, “If the world avoids a recession, it’ll have India and China to thank”, in CNN Business, archived from the original on 08 May 2025:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[169,172]],"id":"a0a48c77-9ea8-4511-9656-8af9fa94a17e"}],"categories":["English initialisms","English terms with quotations","en:United Nations"],"links":[["UN","United Nations"],["International Monetary Fund","International Monetary Fund#English"]],"raw_glosses":["(UN) Initialism of International Monetary Fund."],"qualifier":"UN","glosses":["Initialism of International Monetary Fund."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","initialism"],"alt_of":[{"word":"International Monetary Fund"}],"id":"f2de72cd-353b-4b11-9518-c71d0d42e358"},{"examples":[{"text":"Since 1996 and over six installments, special IMF (The Impossible Missions Force) agent Ethan Hunt (Tom Cruise) has been spectacularly ‘figuring things right in the face of danger, often without a plan.","ref":"2018, Deborah Cornelious, “‘Mission: Impossible - Fallout’ review: mission successful”, in The Hindu, archived from the original on 07 Dec 2022:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[46,49]],"id":"eea2ddf2-88c0-4da7-9e8f-0478f2415167"}],"topics":["fiction","literature","media","publishing"],"categories":["English initialisms","English terms with quotations","en:Fiction"],"links":[["fiction","fiction"],["Impossible Mission Force","w:Impossible Mission Force"]],"raw_glosses":["(fiction) Initialism of Impossible Mission Force, a fictional spy organization from the Mission: Impossible franchise."],"glosses":["Initialism of Impossible Mission Force, a fictional spy organization from the Mission: Impossible franchise."],"tags":["abbreviation","alt-of","initialism"],"alt_of":[{"word":"Impossible Mission Force","extra":"a fictional spy organization from the Mission: Impossible franchise"}],"id":"49d3f9ed-643d-4538-906a-ed8858257be7"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"i'm fine, thank you":{"id":"f71f915e-e0c7-4976-a891-88df204e0308","word":"I'm fine, thank you","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"expected, polite response to how are you?","word":"eu vou bem, obrigado (in response to como vai você?)"}],"pos":"phrase","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["how are you","how are you#English"]],"glosses":["The expected, polite response to how are you?"],"categories":["American Sign Language terms in nonstandard scripts","Arabic terms with non-redundant manual transliterations","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English phrasebook","English phrases","English responses","English sentences","Entries with translation boxes",